.TH LFR 1 "2026-10-30" "Linux Flight Recorder 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lfr \- local evidence-based Linux diagnostic snapshot comparison
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lfr
[\-\-store PATH] [\-\-system] [\-\-config JSON] COMMAND
.SH DESCRIPTION
Records bounded read-only system observations, stores them privately in SQLite,
compares saved snapshots offline and emits reviewed evidence reports.
No automatic repairs, telemetry, sudo invocation or hardware configuration writes.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B snapshot create [\-\-label TEXT] [\-\-source manual|timer|boot|package-event]
Create snapshot. Exit 3 means it was saved with explicit source limitations.
.TP
.B snapshot list|show ID|delete ID|pin ID
List, inspect, delete or protect snapshots. Deleting a pinned snapshot requires
\-\-allow-pinned. IDs are 32 lowercase hexadecimal characters, not labels.
.TP
.B compare BEFORE AFTER [\-\-format text|json]
Offline deterministic comparison; JSON contains full evidence pointers.
.TP
.B report BEFORE AFTER [\-\-symptom wifi|audio|TEXT] \-\-output PATH
Write Markdown report without overwriting an existing path.
.TP
.B export ID \-\-preview
List fixed public bundle members and redaction limitations.
.TP
.B export ID \-\-output bundle.tar.gz
Write redacted diagnostic bundle. Manual privacy review is mandatory.
.TP
.B doctor
Show trusted tool availability and context without collecting a snapshot.
.TP
.B config validate
Validate explicit or default configuration and print effective JSON.
.TP
.B gc [\-\-dry-run]
Plan or apply age/count/logical-size retention, preserving pins.
.SH FILES
$XDG_STATE_HOME/lfr or $HOME/.local/state/lfr for users; /var/lib/lfr for explicit
root \-\-system mode. Private owner-only paths; no symlink store components.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success; 1 runtime/storage error; 2 usage/config error; 3 partial snapshot saved;
130 interrupted by SIGINT/SIGTERM. JSON on stdout, diagnostics on stderr.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Development release. Containers do not validate boot/systemd/hardware support.
Unknown sources are not negative evidence. No causal certainty or full anonymity.
Logical quota excludes SQLite overhead and exported files. Sysfs timeouts are
cooperative and cannot interrupt an uninterruptible kernel read.
.SH SEE ALSO
journalctl(1), systemctl(1), CONFIGURATION.md, PRIVACY.md, docs/VERIFICATION.md
